That's why I had to extricate
myself from the play.


01:15:08.200 --> 01:15:11.795
I mean, that man could
not keep his hands off me.


01:15:13.600 --> 01:15:14.749
Off me.


01:15:16.360 --> 01:15:21.798
Oh, he was a stallion in bed.
He could never get enough.


01:15:22.440 --> 01:15:26.433
<i>And I thought I knew
everything about Kama Sutra.</i>


01:15:27.200 --> 01:15:28.315
Mummy!


01:15:29.880 --> 01:15:33.111
And then, of course,
we became lovers.


01:15:34.840 --> 01:15:37.308
With Jefferson around, none
of my farm animals were safe.


01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:12.437
<i>Tonight, The Stratford Players
present Jefferson Steel in King Lear...</i>


01:16:12.560 --> 01:16:14.755
Four Funerals and a Wedding.


01:16:16.040 --> 01:16:18.429
<i>Tonight, The Stratford
Players present Jefferson...</i>


01:16:21.520 --> 01:16:23.158
Dorothy?
- Yeah.


01:16:23.280 --> 01:16:26.033
Rupert and I had one last thought
about the putting-the-eyes-out scene.


01:16:26.160 --> 01:16:27.275
Right.


01:16:28.480 --> 01:16:29.435
Ooh!


01:16:29.680 --> 01:16:32.353
"Out, vile jelly! Where
is thy lustre now?"


01:16:37.800 --> 01:16:40.758
- Could work.
- Yeah?


01:16:40.880 --> 01:16:43.474
- In a different
play. Okay? Okay.


01:16:44.360 --> 01:16:45.475
Okay.


01:16:48.480 --> 01:16:50.994
- Janine?
- I know, I look a freak.


01:16:51.120 --> 01:16:53.270
You look fantastic!


01:16:54.160 --> 01:16:57.072
- Oh? Do you think so?
- Yeah.


01:17:08.480 --> 01:17:11.756
Okay, "Rusty Steel,
not sharp enough. "


01:17:11.880 --> 01:17:14.713
Very good. What
about this one, right?


01:17:14.840 --> 01:17:17.638
"Tarnished Steel gives
leaden performance. "


01:17:17.760 --> 01:17:21.878
Yes! Okay, let's
watch the show.


01:17:28.240 --> 01:17:30.993
Okay, everyone,
that's 15 minutes.


01:17:31.120 --> 01:17:35.671
Are you ready, Jefferson? How
you feeling? Are you nervous?


01:17:35.800 --> 01:17:38.234
Of course I'm not nervous.


01:17:39.400 --> 01:17:41.118
I... I'm terrified.


01:17:41.240 --> 01:17:44.198
Not a problem. I can do Lear.


01:17:44.320 --> 01:17:45.639
Joke.


01:17:45.760 --> 01:17:48.433
I'm far more
terrified than you are.


01:17:48.560 --> 01:17:52.030
- In fact, I think I'm about to throw up.
- Go, Nigel, go.


01:18:10.080 --> 01:18:15.234
"I thought the king had more affected
the Duke of Albany than Cornwall. "


01:18:15.360 --> 01:18:17.669
"It did always
seem so to us. "


01:18:17.800 --> 01:18:21.713
Let's go out and show them
what a bunch of amateurs can do.


01:18:32.720 --> 01:18:36.030
"Attend the lords of France
and Burgundy, Gloucester. "


01:18:37.320 --> 01:18:38.912
"I shall, my lord. "


01:18:41.160 --> 01:18:45.995
"Meantime, we shall
express our darker purpose.


01:18:46.880 --> 01:18:48.677
"Give me the map there.


01:18:52.360 --> 01:18:56.638
"Know that we have divided
In three our kingdom...


01:18:58.400 --> 01:19:02.359
"and 'tis our fast intent to shake
all cares and business from our age...


01:19:02.480 --> 01:19:06.155
"Conferring them on
younger strengths...


01:19:06.280 --> 01:19:10.193
"while we, unburthen'd,
crawl toward death.


01:19:10.320 --> 01:19:13.995
"Tell me, my daughters,
Which of you shall we say... "


01:19:14.120 --> 01:19:20.036
"Sir, I do love you more than
word can wield the matter...


01:19:20.160 --> 01:19:23.391
"Dearer than eyesight,
space, and liberty. "


01:19:23.520 --> 01:19:26.273
"Poor fool and knave...


01:19:27.080 --> 01:19:31.437
"I have one part in my heart
That's sorry yet for thee. "


01:19:32.760 --> 01:19:37.993
# "He that has and a
little tiny wit... " #


01:19:39.640 --> 01:19:41.756
"O, you are men of stone!


01:19:43.200 --> 01:19:45.236
"Had I your
tongues and eyes...


01:19:45.360 --> 01:19:50.753
"I'd use them so That
heaven's vault would crack.


01:19:53.000 --> 01:19:56.151
"She's gone forever.


01:19:57.320 --> 01:19:59.311
"I might have saved her...


01:20:00.240 --> 01:20:03.118
"now she's gone forever!


01:20:04.240 --> 01:20:08.916
"Cordelia,
Cordelia, why do... "


01:20:12.240 --> 01:20:13.673
Verity?


01:20:13.800 --> 01:20:14.949
Verity?


01:20:16.280 --> 01:20:17.713
Say something.


01:20:18.800 --> 01:20:20.677
She isn't breathing.


01:20:20.800 --> 01:20:22.631
Someone, call
for an ambulance.


01:20:26.120 --> 01:20:28.714
- She's had an allergic reaction.
- She's in anaphylactic shock.


01:20:28.840 --> 01:20:31.877
You're going to need adrenaline, a
laryngoscope, ventilatory support.


01:20:32.000 --> 01:20:34.468
- Are you a doctor?
- No, but I played one in a movie.


01:20:34.600 --> 01:20:37.034
I think we'll take
over from here.


01:20:37.160 --> 01:20:39.276
Oh, watch out for
peri-operative complications.


01:20:39.400 --> 01:20:41.152
Yes, thank you. I'll do that.


01:20:41.280 --> 01:20:42.713
I love you, darling.


01:20:46.800 --> 01:20:48.074
Is she okay?


01:20:48.200 --> 01:20:50.555
You're very lucky, you
got her here just in time.


01:20:50.680 --> 01:20:51.908
She's going to be fine.


01:20:52.040 --> 01:20:55.316
Thank God. In the movie
I did, the kid dies.


01:20:56.440 --> 01:20:59.398
Just a bad reaction to
something she must have eaten.


01:20:59.520 --> 01:21:00.919
There were probably some
nuts in the chocolate.


01:21:01.040 --> 01:21:03.679
Normally, I'm so careful, but what
with the opening night and everything...


01:21:03.800 --> 01:21:04.755
Don't worry.


01:21:04.880 --> 01:21:06.472
She'll need some bed
rest for a few days...


01:21:06.600 --> 01:21:08.556
...but she'll back to her
old self in a week or two.


01:21:08.680 --> 01:21:11.035
- I'll let you know when
she wakes up. Thank you.


01:21:13.560 --> 01:21:14.834
Thank you.


01:21:15.360 --> 01:21:17.316
For giving her the chocolates?


01:21:17.440 --> 01:21:19.158
For saving her life.


01:21:32.560 --> 01:21:35.199
- Miss Nettle, Mr Steel?
- God, what?


01:21:36.640 --> 01:21:38.596
Have you seen the papers?


01:21:38.720 --> 01:21:41.075
- You're the hero of the hour.
- Oh!


01:21:45.200 --> 01:21:46.997
Oh, just look at this review.


01:21:47.960 --> 01:21:51.555
"Startling, brilliant, moving.


01:21:52.560 --> 01:21:54.596
"Steel commands the stage. "


01:21:55.240 --> 01:21:57.959
I haven't had reviews
like that since...


01:22:00.480 --> 01:22:02.436
I never have had
reviews like that.


01:22:02.560 --> 01:22:04.676
And you didn't even
get a curtain call.


01:22:07.120 --> 01:22:08.997
Something else came up.


01:22:09.760 --> 01:22:11.990
With no Cordelia,
we've got no show.


01:22:12.120 --> 01:22:14.680
I'm sorry there
isn't a happy ending.


01:22:15.800 --> 01:22:16.949
Me too.


01:22:17.560 --> 01:22:20.632
I know that life
isn't like that.


01:22:21.840 --> 01:22:23.876
I know it's not
like in the movies.


01:22:24.000 --> 01:22:26.719
Ah, Miss Nettle?
Verity's awake.


01:22:39.400 --> 01:22:41.630
Guess it's time
to say goodbye.


01:22:42.960 --> 01:22:45.235
I'm not very good
at goodbyes...


01:22:46.200 --> 01:22:50.512
...but if ever you're in
Beverly Hills, drop by.


01:22:52.560 --> 01:22:53.834
I mean it.


01:22:56.600 --> 01:22:58.511
- How about Tuesday?
- Ooh, I can't do Tuesday.


01:22:58.640 --> 01:23:00.073
I've got a cesspit to empty.


01:23:00.200 --> 01:23:02.191
- Wednesday?
Wednesday's good for me.


01:23:02.320 --> 01:23:05.995
Mr Steel, can I just say
I'm sorry for everything?


01:23:06.120 --> 01:23:07.758
Particularly for the fact
that you didn't give her one.


01:23:07.880 --> 01:23:09.871
...that night when you
stumbled into her bedroom.


01:23:10.000 --> 01:23:11.877
I'll regret it for
the rest of my life.


01:23:15.080 --> 01:23:18.072
I think it would have
been a night to remember.


01:23:18.240 --> 01:23:19.878
I'll never forgive myself.


01:23:24.480 --> 01:23:25.833
Oh, I'm sorry...


01:23:34.160 --> 01:23:35.434
Thank you.


01:23:38.960 --> 01:23:40.188
Mr Steel?


01:23:42.680 --> 01:23:44.432
It's been a pleasure.


01:23:46.680 --> 01:23:50.195
Come on, Nigel, give us a hug.


01:23:50.320 --> 01:23:53.039
No, Jefferson. You
are still in England.


01:23:57.640 --> 01:24:02.156
It's a shame you have to go. I've
managed to find a new Cordelia.


01:24:13.360 --> 01:24:15.078
"O my dear father!


01:24:17.480 --> 01:24:21.393
"Restoration hang Thy
medicine on my lips...


01:24:21.520 --> 01:24:25.354
"and let this kiss Repair
those violent harms.


01:24:25.480 --> 01:24:29.155
"that my two sisters Have
in thy reverence made. "


01:24:34.840 --> 01:24:36.353
I don't know what to say.


01:24:36.480 --> 01:24:38.152
Oh, I think you do.


01:24:41.440 --> 01:24:44.989
"Pray, do not mock me...


01:24:48.600 --> 01:24:54.311
"for I am a very
foolish, fond old man.


01:24:55.160 --> 01:24:57.355
"Do not laugh at me...


01:24:57.480 --> 01:25:02.998
"For, as I am a man, I think
this lady To be my child. "


01:25:04.400 --> 01:25:08.234
"And so I am, I am. "


01:25:17.360 --> 01:25:18.952
Thank you.


01:25:19.240 --> 01:25:21.071
You can thank Verity.


01:25:21.200 --> 01:25:23.395
She was the one who thought
Amanda might have some insight.


01:25:23.520 --> 01:25:25.670
...into playing the
daughter of a madman.


01:25:27.400 --> 01:25:29.550
So, shall we rehearse?


01:25:33.400 --> 01:25:38.838
"Be your tears wet?
I pray weep not.


01:25:39.960 --> 01:25:44.238
"If you have poison
for me, I will drink it.


01:25:46.520 --> 01:25:50.877
"I know you do not love
me, for your sisters.


01:25:51.000 --> 01:25:57.269
"Have, as I do
remember, done me wrong.


01:25:59.240 --> 01:26:01.629
"You have some cause...


01:26:04.360 --> 01:26:06.237
"they have not. "


01:26:07.160 --> 01:26:08.878
"No cause...


01:26:10.680 --> 01:26:12.318
"no cause. "


01:26:19.160 --> 01:26:23.950
"I might have saved her,
and now she's gone...


01:26:26.160 --> 01:26:28.037
"... forever.


01:26:30.840 --> 01:26:37.154
"Cordelia, Cordelia,
stay a little.


01:26:40.800 --> 01:26:42.597
"What is't thou say'st?


01:26:44.720 --> 01:26:49.032
"Her voice was ever soft.


01:26:49.160 --> 01:26:50.593
"and gentle.


01:26:52.520 --> 01:26:54.351
"and low...


01:26:55.680 --> 01:26:59.355
"an excellent
thing in woman. "


01:27:00.400 --> 01:27:04.234
"The weight of this
sad time we must obey...


01:27:04.360 --> 01:27:08.558
"Speak what we feel,
not what we ought to say.


01:27:08.680 --> 01:27:10.716
"The oldest hath borne most.


01:27:11.480 --> 01:27:18.318
"We that are young Shall never
see so much, nor live so long. "


01:27:24.880 --> 01:27:26.279
Bravo!


01:27:27.040 --> 01:27:28.314
Bravo!


01:27:28.440 --> 01:27:29.589
- Enjoy that?
- Yeah.


01:27:31.000 --> 01:27:34.788
I told you it works
better in a bigger venue.


01:27:34.920 --> 01:27:36.478
You really are mad.


01:27:36.600 --> 01:27:38.192
What's the point in being a
movie star if you can't hire.


01:27:38.320 --> 01:27:40.550
...the Old Vic
for a few nights?


01:27:41.200 --> 01:27:42.519
Bravo!


01:27:43.320 --> 01:27:44.435
Bravo!


01:27:45.880 --> 01:27:47.313
Bravo!


01:27:51.640 --> 01:27:55.030
Hey, Dorothy, what are
we gonna do next year?


01:27:55.280 --> 01:27:57.714
- Next year?
- But the theatre's saved.


01:27:57.840 --> 01:28:00.229
You don't really
have to come back.


01:28:00.360 --> 01:28:03.432
<i>- How about Richard III?
- Yeah, you're good at sequels.</i>


01:28:03.560 --> 01:28:05.630
<i>Then Richard llI it is.</i>


01:28:05.760 --> 01:28:09.548
- What's that about again?
- It's about power and seduction.


01:28:09.680 --> 01:28:12.069
Well, I'll have to
do some research.


01:28:16.160 --> 01:28:18.628
He's coming back
over my dead body.


01:28:19.200 --> 01:28:20.633
Bravo!

